From 75bbf1a11bcdf47528cf127f802cb1e4e4158059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][player information] Frame packing named and shown in
 its raster, and a 3D output the display is not told of

The player information said the mode of a frame-packed 3D output as its 2D
timing, "1920x1080 @ 23.976 Hz", and nothing of the 3D output: the
display gets one frame of both eyes and the lines between them, 1920x2205
(issue 33, forum thread 30682 #172 and #207). Where the driver did not take
frame packing, the eyes went out over/under in an ordinary 2D mode, and
nothing said that the display was not told of 3D.

STEREO::ShownOf() decides what the 3D output is from what goes out: the
layout of the mode that the kernel says the output is in (a mode that the
driver refused is not it), else the HDMI vendor InfoFrame of a half layout
that the driver has from Kodi, else the eyes drawn split and nothing told.
CWinSystemGbm::StereoOutputShown() reads it on the thread that draws, and
the player information publishes it as hades.out.stereo; a frame-packed
mode is said in its raster (STEREO::ScanoutHeight(): 1920x2205 at 1080p24,
1280x1470 at 720p50/60). The overview says the mode and the 3D output in
one line ("1920x2205 @ 23.976 Hz, 3D frame packing", "..., 3D not told"),
and the output page has a row 3D that says it in full, with what to do
where the display is not told. In 2D nothing changes. The NVIDIA refusal
of frame packing itself is not touched here.

The strings are in English, Spanish (Spain), Spanish (Argentina) and
Spanish (Mexico); system/hades is made again by make-playerinfo.py.
